# Agda
_build/
*.agdai

# Python developer-tooling virtual environment (created by `make venv` from
# requirements-dev.txt; never committed). Python bytecode caches.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Cloudflare wrangler local cache/state
.wrangler/

# Claude Code: owner-private, kept local only, never committed/pushed (default; only
# commit anything here if the owner explicitly asks).
.claude/

# A PROBE IS TRACKED, and its home is agents/tasks/<TASK>/, beside the report
# it belongs to (dev/LESSONS.md D-1, owner's ruling 2026-08-13). NOTHING BELOW
# IGNORES IT THERE, and that is deliberate.
#
# What is ignored is a probe under src/, which is forbidden absolutely. That
# rule was bought on 2026-08-04, when one `git add -A src/` committed 13 probe
# files, 3,274 lines. An ignore rule is a default and `git add -f` walks past
# it; scripts/check-probes.py is the gate.
#
# EVERY .agda under src/ is a probe by construction: masters are .lagda.md,
# and `git ls-files` finds zero tracked .agda there. A probe named anything
# else slipped past the Probe* pattern once (src/MetaTest.agda, 2026-08-13).
src/**/*.agda
src/**/*.agdai
src/Probe*.agda
src/Probe*.agdai
# [LJ-1.72] wrote its probes as .lagda.md, which this list did not cover, so
# check-fences counted five probes as masters (89 against 84). check-probes
# already knew the shape; only the ignore list was blind.
src/Probe*.lagda.md
